        "uuid": "f86af8de_c7d23840",
        "filename": "common/system_boot_time.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1523717
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-28T01:39:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Setting ap_booted\u003dfalse here will not help in identifying the warm reboot scenario. In warm reboot case, the seq of event is PLTRST_LOW and then PLTRST_HIGH, setting ap_booted\u003dfalse in PLTRST_LOW results ap_boot_time.cnt \u003d 0 in PLTRST_HIGH which cause failure in identifying warm reboot scenario.\n\nBecause of the above reason ap_booted is set to false in RESET_CNT scenario, RESET_CNT will be triggered when from system_common_shutdown when during hook notify HOOK_CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE",
      "parentUuid": "7564367c_6e47f7c2",
